; windtrap_coverage is the coverage seam's data source: the runner
; snapshots in-process coverage at run end for the inline summary, and
; the driver builds the report's section data from it. windtrap_mutate
; is the mutation seam's: the mutation loop and the CLI spell mutant
; identifiers and the arming variable with the runtime's own functions
; before they enter section data, so the report and the runtime cannot
; disagree about what to type — Render draws sections and names neither
; runtime. Both dependencies point downward only — neither runtime
; links windtrap.

(library
 (name windtrap)
 (public_name windtrap)
 (libraries unix windtrap_coverage windtrap_mutate)
 ; Windtrap measures its own coverage. The backend is spelled
 ; `ppx_windtrap.coverage`, not the `ppx_windtrap` the manual shows
 ; users: that name resolves to the inline-test rewriter, whose
 ; ppx_runtime_libraries would put ppx_windtrap.runtime — and through it
 ; this very library — into its own closure, which is a dependency cycle.
 ; See ppx/coverage/dune. Inert without --instrument-with: a plain
 ; `dune runtest` builds and runs exactly as before.
 (instrumentation
  (backend ppx_windtrap.coverage))
 ; And windtrap mutates itself. Six modules opt out with
 ; [@@@mutate exclude_file] — the scheduler, the ambient run state, the
 ; reporting spine — because a mutant there is armed inside the process
 ; that is supposed to judge it, and the failure mode is a hang rather
 ; than a survivor. The loop and the inline runtime, excluded for the
 ; same reason, live above the core (lib/mutation, ppx/runtime) in
 ; libraries whose dune carries no mutation stanza at all.
 ;
 ; This stanza is only safe because of WINDTRAP_MUTATE_ONLY. The tree's
 ; own mutation suites are built on controlled catalogues — a zero-mutant
 ; control executable, a fixture of exactly five sites — and an
 ; instrumented core would otherwise hand them 984 more. They name their
 ; scope, so they keep a GENUINE catalogue rather than a simulated one.
 ; See doc/dev/testing.md.
 (instrumentation
  (backend ppx_windtrap.mutate))
 (foreign_stubs
  (language c)
  (names capture_stubs clock_stubs env_stubs)))
